strings.SUR_forpol.24.desc:
UNDERSTANDING concerns over the process of independence that a prospective Surinamese Republic with the wider circumstances of administration and of the Netherlands' unique geographic position,
NOTING that the Kingdom of the Netherlands is still mostly occupied by the Greater German Reich, and calling for its full independence to be restored by Germania as per Resolution 04/1947,
RECOGNISING the risk that economic and geographical insecurity poses to the people within the Netherlands, and to those within Suriname,
EMPHASISING the importance of Article 4, that ideals of popular sovereignty and democracy are central tenets within the foundation of this alliance,
HIGHLIGHTING wider issues with discrimination and inequality in the Netherlands on a racial level,

The Organisation of Free Nations hereby;
1. Indefinitely suspends Dutch membership until its military junta is dissolved, alongside all military cooperation;
2. Calls for the referendum on Surinamese independence to be respected and for the pardoning of nationalists currently imprisoned;
3. Backs the repeal of laws preventing people of certain races from fully partaking in all aspects of Dutch society;
4. Encourages all members within to take swift action to ensure that all of these tenets are fully implemented.
